 5. 💼 AI roils the job hunt 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Gabriella Turrisi/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Technology has made it easier for people to apply for jobs — and for employers to screen them out, Axios' Josephine Walker reports. 

 AI usage is rampant on both sides: Applicants can automate applications and spray them out, while employers use tech to sort through the flood. By the numbers: Recruiters process roughly 291 applications per hire, up from about 100 in early 2021, per recruiting firm Ashby. 

 About 63% of U.S. applicants have been interviewed by a bot, while 38% say they've walked away from a job because it included an AI interview. 👻 What we're watching: Ghost jobs, or jobs companies aren't actively trying to fill, make up about 18–22% of posted jobs in a typical quarter, per internal Greenhouse data.

